The types and semantics of C (T3b), on cparse's tree (tools/c.ff): the type of every declaration and expression (typedefs and typeof resolved),
the integer promotions and the usual arithmetic conversions, array and function decay, lvalues, the implicit casts made explicit with clang's kinds,
sizeof and alignof, struct and union layout as the target's ABI lays them out (riscv64, x86_64, aarch64, arm), integer constant expressions folded,
string literals and their types, initializers in their semantic form (every field, brace elision, designators), as clang's Sema builds them for C.
Its dev source is C (tools/dev/cs, tools/dev/mk.sh), made ff by gen/c2ff.pl. Checked against clang (gen/csemacheck.sh): its JSON AST and record layouts.
T3c, on the same tree: its statements kept, as gen/c2ff.pl's expr and stmt the C layer of what a unit's roots reach, its types (ctype, the tags' names), its asm statements and syscall idiom per target,
long double's literals rounded and folded, gen/Words.pm's words of now and gen/Header.pm's license nodes: csema -l. Checked against c2ff.pl unit by unit, byte for byte (gen/clayercheck.sh).
